attributes.description:
A vendor-neutral record of the web applications an access gateway or agent protects (core domain webaccess, branch ou=protected-applications). Each application (ciamProtectedApp) records:
- its base path and the service-name roles it is published as;
- the server role enforcing it, overridable per environment to move it to another product;
- the backend role behind a gateway;
- sign-on: kind, integration, identity service and credential role;
- session idle/max;
- the header contracts it sets;
- its access rules.
Its path resources (ciamPathResource) carry pattern, match kind prefix|wildcard|regex, methods, access mode standard|anonymous|unprotected, order and rules. Access rules (ciamAccessRule) carry allow|deny|custom, who-expressions, any|all and included rules.
The PingAccess, SiteMinder and PingGateway importers project their objects onto it, owning only what they projected (ciamProjectedFrom).
The core planner check covers:
- an application left unprotected in the target;
- a cross-product move's prerequisites (published and backend roles, sign-in integration, header setter with fix enforcer-header);
- the fix protect:<adapter>/<app>.
Product checks report what their product can't express (webaccess.losses over capabilities declared as data). PingAccess and PingGateway render the neutral applications enforced by their roles that they hold no native entry for. Report protected-applications.
